messages:
Laura Chen: Kicking off a combined PRD + RFC thread for KV-cache eviction + kernel-fallback behavior. Customer asks (FinServ-Alpha) require stable p95 latency and no output-quality regressions for multi-turn chat. Need scope, acceptance criteria, and rollout plan.

Mike O'Neill: +1. We should define kernel selection rules first (latency-first vs cost-first) and a strict fallback mapping so requests never block. Example: if int8 kernel missing, fallback to fp16 on a different device pool.

Anita Gupta: Draft acceptance criteria from PM side: 1) p95 latency <= 80ms under baseline workload (50 req/s, seq=1024) 2) end-to-end quality (BLEU/ROUGE/P@1 for rank) not drop >1% vs current model 3) no more than 0.1% error-rate (OOMs, timeouts) during rollout 4) canary to 5% -> 25% -> 100% with automated rollback triggers.

Raj Patel: Edge cases we need to call out: long KV chains where prefix cache hits but suffix misses, partial KV corruption (missing embeddings), mixed-precision mismatch when KV stored in quantized format but kernel expects fp16, and multi-actor calls (tool-calling + streaming). Also consider cross-variant routing: model-v2quant -> model-v2fp16 fallback.

Emily Zhao: Ops notes: We need detailed tracing on per-token latency and per-request fallback reason. Also a roll-forward metric: fraction of requests served by fallback kernel per minute. Alert if fallback fraction > 2% for 10m. Canary automation should enforce baseline traffic isolation.

Dan Morales: Proposed KV eviction config samples for perf tests:```json
{
  "kv_eviction_policy": "LRU",
  "max_entries": 500000,
  "prefix_cache_enabled": true,
  "staleness_ttl_ms": 60000,
  "write_through": false
}
```Run perf matrix: varying max_entries {50k,200k,500k} x batch_size {1,8,32} x seq_len {256,1024}. Capture p50/p95 and mem usage.

Mike O'Neill: For kernel selection heuristics, propose: priority list per-model: [optimized-int8, optimized-fp16, generic-fp16]. Selection key = (model_arch, seq_len_bucket, requested_latency_tier). If optimized kernel not loaded -> try warm-start prefetch of kernels for hot models during low-traffic windows.

Laura Chen: Scope negotiation: MVP (Q2) = eviction policy + deterministic fallback mapping + canary automation + perf harness + simple rollout docs. NO: auto-quantization or live kernel compiling (defer to Q3). Customer-visible launch criteria = acceptance criteria from Anita + runbook + support SLA notes.

Anita Gupta: Acceptance tests (concrete): - Synthetic replay with FinServ-Alpha dataset must meet p95 SLA for 3/3 runs. - Regression eval: run 10k prompts comparing outputs, flagged diffs reviewed. - Chaos test: randomly simulate kernel unload and verify fallback <= 200ms additional latency 99% of time.

Raj Patel: Edge-case handling pseudocode to include in RFC:
```
if (kernel_missing) {
  route_to: fallback_kernel;
  increment(fallback_counter);
  emit(trace, "fallback_reason", reason);
}
if (kv_entry_missing && prefix_hit) {
  do_prefetch(prefix_key);
  mark_realtime_miss();
}
```

Emily Zhao: Rollout playbook: canary 5% for 4hr -> check metrics (p95, error-rate, fallback fraction) -> if green, 25% for 6hr -> 100% over 24hr. Auto-rollback triggers: p95 regression >10% or error-rate spike >0.5% or fallback fraction >5% sustained.

Mike O'Neill: Performance knobs to expose in console for Dedicated customers: max_entries, prefix_cache_ttl_ms, kernel_priority_list, fallback_latency_threshold_ms. Keep defaults conservative.

Laura Chen: Next steps: Mike/ Raj to draft a short RFC with kernel mapping table + pseudocode by EOD Friday. Dan/Emily to run baseline perf test matrix and attach artifacts. Anita to prepare acceptance criteria in PRD doc and liaise with FinServ-Alpha for dataset. I'll schedule a 30m review on Monday. Any objections?

deploy-bot: scheduled: #infra-perf-test -> started job 987654321 (tags: kv-evict-matrix).

Dan Morales: noted, starting run now. Will post perf gist when done.

Raj Patel: one more note — if we allow model-variant fallback across regions, we need to consider tokenization compatibility and reproducibility. Add that to the RFC.

Laura Chen: Good catch. Added. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
